WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:03.710
It's a tough world out there in the TV industry.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:07.859
For every megahit, there's another show that
fails to find an audience.

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:13.540
Sometimes, it's a reflection on a series'
quality, but in the era of peak TV, that isn't

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:14.710
always the case.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:20.000
Often, great TV flies under the radar due
to the sheer amount of content viewers have

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.500
to choose from every week.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.880
With that in mind, let's take a look at why
these shows were canceled in 2018.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.640
Ash vs. Evil Dead

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.910
Starz canceled Ash vs. Evil Dead in April,
allowing the story to wrap up with the third

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.160
season finale.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.480
A follow-up to Sam Raimi's Evil Dead films,
the series brought back Bruce Campbell as

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.540
the titular demon slayer.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.270
Campbell seemed willing to go on playing Ash
forever, calling it "the role of a lifetime,"

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:53.219
but Starz pulled the plug in an effort to
refine its slate of scripted originals.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:01:00.030
The series launched with 437,000 same-day
viewers, but its ratings fell over its run,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.609
eventually dropping to just 175,000.

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:08.390
Although those numbers probably jumped when
DVR views were added in, that's still a disappointing

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:12.770
figure for an established property with a
big name star.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.660
The Exorcist

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:20.870
Fox's supernatural drama The Exorcist, a sequel
to the 1973 film of the same name, starred

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:25.480
Alfonso Herrera and Ben Daniels as a pair
of priests searching for evil.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:30.080
It was well-received by critics, but it never
pulled in huge audience numbers.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:36.830
The second season averaged just 1.9 million
viewers and only a 0.6 rating in the key 18-to-49

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.900
demo.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.140
Although many fans were upset, showrunner
Jeremy Slater said that they shouldn't blame

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.920
the network for its decision.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:44.920
He tweeted,

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.910
"I know it's easy to get angry at Fox, but
the reality is that we were the lowest-rated

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:53.140
drama on any network and they still brought
us back for a second season, because they

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.410
loved the show.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.030
There are no bad guys in this scenario."

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.070
The Last Man on Earth

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:04.460
Fox sitcom The Last Man on Earth had its last
season on Earth in 2018.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:08.880
It starred Will Forte as the lone survivor
of a lethal, worldwide virus.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.620
Or at least he seemed to be alone at first.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:16.530
He was eventually joined by other survivors,
including characters played by Kristen Schaal,

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:21.810
January Jones, Mel Rodriguez, Cleopatra Coleman,
and Mary Steenburgen.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:26.970
The fourth and final season ended on a cliffhanger,
leaving fans hugely disappointed.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:31.820
The series was the casualty of a Fox comedy
blitz, as the network canceled all of its

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:32.950
live-action sitcoms.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:38.590
The show did earn five Emmy nominations over
its run, including two for Forte, but that

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.480
wasn't enough to keep it on the air.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.230
It's enough to make you sick.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:48.920
"Oh my God."

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.400
Lucifer

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:56.460
The devil was officially out at Fox in 2018
when the network canceled Lucifer after three

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.460
seasons.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.380
The show starred Tom Ellis as the fallen angel,
who had retired from Hell and moved to Los

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:06.840
Angeles, working double duty as a nightclub
owner and a consultant for the LAPD.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:13.990
Although Lucifer averaged just 4.1 million
viewers and a 1.1 rating in the 18 to 49 demo

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:18.990
in its last season, it was still beloved by
fans, who immediately started campaigning

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.150
to find a new home for the drama.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:25.930
Their enthusiasm paid off, as Netflix picked
up Lucifer for a fourth season.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:29.010
Sometimes it pays to make a deal with the
devil.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.010
The Mick

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:34.709
Kaitlin Olson has enjoyed a long run on It's
Always Sunny in Philadelphia…

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:40.060
"Say guys, what's the deal with those hands
free headsets that everybody's wearing in

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.330
their ears right?"

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:48.250
...but her luck wasn't quite as good for her
Fox sitcom The Mick, which was canceled after

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.900
just two seasons.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:54.710
Olson played Mickey, an irresponsible wild
child who gets stuck with taking care of her

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.050
sister's rich, spoiled children.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:01.790
Although The Mick received a mostly positive
critical reception, it failed to build on

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:06.790
its mild buzz, averaging just 3.1 million
viewers over its two seasons.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:10.770
That might have been good enough for renewal
in a normal year, but with Fox's acquisition

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:15.420
of NFL Thursday Night Football, the network
had much less space on its schedule.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:18.250
The Mick was just one of several casualties.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:23.590
"Mickey, it was one thing when you were squatting
in our mansion but now you're costing us money."

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:24.590
"Alright, alright."

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.090
Mozart in the Jungle

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:32.430
Amazon left the music behind in 2018, canceling
its drama Mozart in the Jungle after four

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.430
seasons.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:39.710
Based on oboist Blair Tindall's 2005 memoir,
the show starred Gael Garcia Bernal as the

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.960
new conductor of the New York Symphony.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.780
The show was critically acclaimed, winning
Golden Globes for Best Series and Best Actor

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.800
for Bernal in 2016.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.400
Its cancellation comes as Amazon tries to
shift its programming towards bigger dramas

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.690
with more international appeal, in the vein
of HBO's massively successful Game of Thrones.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:03.419
Mozart was just the first casualty of this
new directive.

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:05.100
Once Upon a Time

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:10.460
ABC's fairy tale drama Once Upon a Time has
lost a lot of viewers over the years, but

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:15.100
it managed to stay popular enough with a loyal
group of fans to earn an unexpected seventh

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.540
season renewal in 2017.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:21.970
That renewal also came with a massive creative
overhaul, with much of the principal cast

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.590
replaced by newcomers.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:28.390
Despite the reboot, Once Upon a Time still
struggled in the ratings, and Season 7 became

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.889
its last.

00:05:29.889 --> 00:05:34.110
ABC Entertainment President Channing Dungey
called it a "bittersweet" goodbye.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:39.280
With the show averaging 2.5 million viewers,
down 20 percent from the year before, the

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:42.290
writing was clearly on the wall.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:43.290
The Path

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:49.050
It seemed like Hulu landed something big with
The Path, starring a fresh-off-Breaking-Bad

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:54.199
Aaron Paul and Golden Globe nominee Michelle
Monaghan as husband-and-wife members of a

00:05:54.199 --> 00:05:55.600
cult-like religion.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.780
Despite the series' impressive pedigree, it
only lasted three seasons.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:04.370
Hulu doesn't release ratings, so it's unclear
what kind of viewership the show was pulling

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:08.190
in, but it never received the critical acclaim
to match its premise and cast.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:13.250
While it garnered decent reviews, the fact
that it never received any major awards nominations

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.389
was probably the nail in the coffin.

00:06:15.389 --> 00:06:20.250
The leads' expensive paychecks probably didn't
help either.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.250
Roseanne

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:26.390
ABC's Roseanne reboot was met with controversy
right out of the gate, thanks to star Roseanne

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:31.160
Barr's politics, which eventually led to the
sitcom getting pulled off the air.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:36.169
ABC reversed its initial renewal decision
after Barr tweeted racist and Islamophobic

00:06:36.169 --> 00:06:39.760
statements about former White House advisor
Valerie Jarrett.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:44.720
Announcing the show's cancellation, ABC Entertainment
President Channing Dungey said,

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:49.880
"Roseanne's Twitter statement is abhorrent,
repugnant and inconsistent with our values,

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.980
and we have decided to cancel her show."

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.410
"I was being nice!

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:54.740
She's a crazy, stupid hillbilly!"

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:59.900
It was a stunning decision, considering that
Roseanne was the highest rated scripted show

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:05.410
on broadcast television that season, averaging
19.3 million viewers.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:10.410
Ultimately, those numbers were too good for
ABC to let go of completely: a Roseanne-free

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.280
spinoff, dubbed The Conners, was announced
in late June.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.979
Shades of Blue

00:07:15.979 --> 00:07:20.800
Jennifer Lopez's star power wasn't enough
to keep her cop drama Shades of Blue on the

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.800
air.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:27.670
Starring Lopez as a single mother and NYPD
detective recruited to work on the FBI's anti-corruption

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.639
task force, the show was canceled after three
seasons.

00:07:30.639 --> 00:07:33.600
The final season is currently airing over
the summer.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:39.020
Lopez, who also serves as an executive producer,
has said that there will be a "poetic three-season

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.419
arc" to the way her character's story ends.

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:45.800
Although averaging seven million viewers in
Season 2, it seems that keeping a star as

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:49.870
pricey as Lopez wasn't worth it for NBC.

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:51.210
Taken

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:55.870
Being based on a well-known film series isn't
enough to ensure a TV show's success.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:00.310
Such was the case for the NBC drama Taken,
a prequel to the Liam Neeson flicks of the

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:01.310
same name.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:05.850
The show, which starred Clive Standen as a
younger version of Neeson's Bryan Mills, was

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.310
canceled after airing two seasons.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:12.930
It followed Mills during his days as a former
Green Beret and member of an elite team of

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:17.930
covert operatives tasked with conducting dangerous
rescue missions around the world.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:23.449
After a lackluster critical reception in season
one, Taken experienced a major cast overhaul

00:08:23.449 --> 00:08:27.300
and brought on a new showrunner for year two,
but that wasn't enough.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:32.070
The show was NBC's lowest-rated drama in the
18 to 49 demo.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:37.439
Mills may have a very special set of skills,
but bringing in viewers apparently isn't one

00:08:37.439 --> 00:08:39.319
of them.

00:08:39.319 --> 00:08:40.319
Timeless

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:45.569
Timeless came back from cancellation once,
but it couldn't pull off that same trick twice.The

00:08:45.569 --> 00:08:51.410
show starred Abigail Spencer, Malcolm Barrett,
and Matt Lanter as a history professor, scientist,

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:56.160
and soldier tasked with traveling through
time to prevent the alteration of history.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:00.649
It struggled in the ratings from the get-go,
and thanks to an expensive budget due, to

00:09:00.649 --> 00:09:05.980
constant changes in costumes and settings,
NBC decided to pull the plug after its first

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:06.980
season.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:10.850
However, the network wound up reversing that
decision just a few days later, after fan

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:14.509
outcry from viewers who dubbed themselves
"Clockblockers."

00:09:14.509 --> 00:09:18.970
Although those fans were just as active on
social media calling for a renewal after season

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:25.019
two's cliffhanger ending, NBC ultimately canceled
the show again thanks to continued lackluster

00:09:25.019 --> 00:09:26.019
ratings.

00:09:26.019 --> 00:09:27.509
And this time, it looks like it's permanent.

